From 433a5f064b13369c4b7840a39c8d7debd4e7d25c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:56:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(update): active-work carries the checkpoint's
 own verdict; a refused pause announces no restart

example-host 2026-11-12 18:11Z: at the instant cap hermes-sync's census read
`active=7 units=7 (cron,managed)`, saw no unpreservable kind and launched the
updater; the gateway then refused the checkpoint ("unpreservable work: 1 chat
turn (active=7, preservable managed=3, cron=3)"). Three units were Kanban cards
and three cut cron runs; the seventh was an executing turn outside
`_running_agents` that `_describe_active_work` pads in as a sessionless
`managed` unit (`uncounted_runtime_work_units`), which `kanban_managed_count`
rightly does not preserve. Unit kinds cannot carry the checkpoint's predicate.

- update_checkpoint.checkpoint_work(runner, cron_cut): the checkpoint's count
  check as one dict (active, preservable_managed, cron, preservable);
  checkpoint_for_update uses it.
- The unscoped `active-work` answer carries it as `checkpoint` (cron cut), so
  an updater census decides with the same predicate. Omitted when unreadable.
- The refusal names work outside its probes as "N other unit(s) (an unmapped
  turn, a side agent or a managed turn that is not a Kanban card)" and names
  chat-turn session keys again: `_running_agents` on GatewayRunner is a live
  SessionFieldView (a Mapping), not a dict, so the keys were always dropped.
- update_cmd_posix_pause: when every gateway refused the pause (each left the
  set via mark_stop_refused) print "No gateway was stopped ...; nothing to
  restart" instead of "Recovery: restarting the stopped gateways on the old
  code"; the settle call still runs.

Tests: test_update_checkpoint_census_agreement.py drives real GatewayRunner
accounting through the hub's 18:11:25Z shape (census and refusal agree, before
and after the turn's agent is mapped; cards + cut cron preservable; a non-card
managed turn unpreservable; unreadable verdict omitted) and
test_a_refused_pause_announces_no_restart runs the real _stop_gateways and
mark_stop_refused. 5 of the 7 new tests fail on main.

Card t_01a1d106ee4eacff.
